<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhupinder Singh of Patiala</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1891">1891</a>–<a href="/years/1938">1938</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bhupinder Singh was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of Patiala, the leading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> princely state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, from 1900 to 1938. Famous for his lavish lifestyle and jewels, including the Patiala Necklace made by Cartier, he was also a keen cricketer and patron who captained an Indian team in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in 1911. He served several terms as Chancellor of the Chamber of Princes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bhupinder-singh-of-patiala.jpg" alt="Bhupinder Singh of Patiala" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhupinder_Singh_of_Patiala.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
